From e2ee1a249a14c5839f90ffb1a9ded4889e70f1b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:35:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix: require admin auth on all /api/admin/* routes

Next.js middleware only guards /dashboard/admin/* page routes, not
/api/admin/* API routes, so every admin API endpoint was reachable
without authentication. This adds a shared requireAdmin() guard
(lib/admin-auth.ts) that verifies the JWT access token and checks
role === "admin", and wires it into all 11 previously-unprotected
routes: stats, error-logs, error-logs/[id], audit-logs, users/bulk,
users/bulk-email, events, events/[id], events/[id]/approve,
campaigns, and campaigns/[id]/send.

Also, while adding the guard:
- Removed a dead  in
  audit-logs/route.ts guarding a commented-out check; next-auth was
  never a project dependency, so this would have thrown if the
  commented code were ever restored as-is.
- Replaced several client-supplied adminId / hardcoded
  "admin@system.com" values used in audit-log entries with the
  actual authenticated admin's id/email.
- Fixed an audit log call using "event_approved"/"event_rejected",
  which are not valid values in the AuditLog schema's action enum
  (would throw a Mongoose validation error); logs as "event_updated"
  with the outcome recorded in details instead.
