From 2c7b4233de2ef4400ace30eadc482e19a7f504ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:35:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Redesign: new landing page visual identity

Full rewrite of app/page.tsx, replacing the generic gradient-blob/
glassmorphism hero with a design grounded in the actual product
(GSU student clubs), inspired structurally by a fintech landing
page reference but restyled around campus/club subject matter:

- Palette: ink #181a22, warm paper #f8f4ea, marigold #f0a93b /
  #cf8a1f, coral #e35c55, forest green #26594a
- Type: Space Grotesk (display) + IBM Plex Sans (body) via
  next/font/google
- Structural motif: a campus ID-badge card style (notch tab, pin
  dot) reused across the hero visual, feature mockups, and the
  three role-based panels
- Sections: hero -> scrolling fact strip -> stat band -> three
  alternating feature panels (clubs / newsfeed / events, each tied
  to real model behavior like the event approval workflow and
  admin audit log) -> "why Connectrix" grid -> role paths
  (Student / Club / Admin, replacing a generic pricing section
  since the product has no paid tiers) -> FAQ accordion -> CTA
  band -> footer
- No fabricated usage metrics (e.g. no invented "75K+ users"
  style stat) -- the stat band only uses verifiable catalog facts
  (faculty/department counts)

Verified with a full production ; all existing routes
and the new page compile cleanly.
